# secrets.env.example — copy to secrets.env and fill in.  DO NOT COMMIT secrets.env.
#
#   cp secrets.env.example secrets.env
#   chmod 600 secrets.env
#
# Format: KEY=value  (shell-sourceable; no quotes needed, no spaces around `=`).
# run.sh sources this for Telegram delivery; tools/proxy.js reads the PROXY_*
# keys directly (it parses this file itself, so the proxy works even though
# run.sh launches node before sourcing this file).

# ---- Telegram delivery (optional) -----------------------------------------
TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN=
TELEGRAM_CHAT_ID=

# ---- Residential proxy (optional) -----------------------------------------
# Used to give scrapers an Indian residential exit IP. When PROXY_URL is set,
# scrapers wired to tools/proxy.js (currently: zepto) route their browser
# through it. When PROXY_URL is BLANK or these lines stay commented, scrapers
# run DIRECT (no proxy) — unchanged behaviour.
#
# Recommended provider: IPRoyal residential (pay-as-you-go, India exit IPs).
# Gateway host:port is geo.iproyal.com:12321 . India + sticky-session targeting
# is encoded in the PASSWORD using IPRoyal's _key-value suffixes:
#   _country-in                 -> Indian exit IP
#   _session-XXXXXXXX           -> sticky session id (8 alphanumeric chars)
#   _lifetime-10m               -> keep that IP for 10 minutes (max 7d)
# Drop _session/_lifetime to get a fresh rotating IP on every request.
# See docs/PROXY.md for the full per-platform rotation guidance.
#
# Two ways to set it — pick ONE:
#
# A) Separate fields (recommended; keeps the password readable):
# PROXY_URL=http://geo.iproyal.com:12321
# PROXY_USERNAME=your_iproyal_username
# PROXY_PASSWORD=your_iproyal_password_country-in_session-a1b2c3d4_lifetime-10m
#
# B) Everything embedded in one URL (creds are split out automatically):
# PROXY_URL=http://your_iproyal_username:your_iproyal_password_country-in_session-a1b2c3d4_lifetime-10m@geo.iproyal.com:12321
